# Hauntwoods Shrieker: "Whenever this creature attacks, manifest dread." and "{1}{G}: Reveal target face-down permanent. If it's a
# creature card, you may turn it face up." (CR 701.62a, 701.20a, 701.40b, 708.2a, 708.8).
#
# Turn 1: Black Lotus (green) pays {1}{G}{G} for the Shrieker; the Moxen are left untapped. Turn 3 the Shrieker attacks: the trigger
# manifests dread, Snapcaster Mage going onto the battlefield face down as a 2/2 and Lightning Bolt into the graveyard. After combat
# the ability ({1}{G} from Mox Jet and Mox Emerald) targets that face-down permanent: Snapcaster Mage is a creature card, so Bot1 is
# asked and turns it face up. It is the same permanent, a 2/1 with flash, and it is not entering, so its enters trigger doesn't happen.

